 real structural difference ... repack ... hang below it.'","AC4: '`make verify` is green on the Linux CI gate (`Verified +1` on the Gerrit change)' — runs on a different git than the one where the sid-hierarchy was measured.","The detector test (step 5) and the primary assertion (step 4) both depend on sid-nesting behavior that is a git-version-dependent runtime characteristic, not a stable advertised contract."],"finding":"The new proving mechanism relies on Git Trace2 sid-hierarchy semantics (a child `git maintenance`/`repack` process gets a sid prefixed by the parent commit's sid plus '/') and on auto-maintenance spawning as a descendant of `git commit`. This structural behavior was empirically validated only on the investigation host (macOS/Git 2.56), but AC4 ('make verify green on the Linux CI gate') and the detector test's determinism execute against the Linux CI's git version, where Trace2 event format or the auto-maintenance-as-child spawn behavior could differ — the plan does not state a minimum/assumed Git version or verify the trace behavior on the CI git.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbb158a759c905a4e","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach steps 3-5; Acceptance Criteria line 4 ('make verify is green on the Linux CI gate')","norm_id":"ne852b30d21b7899c","priority":0.2933,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["CI git version emits Trace2 events whose sid nesting differs, making the descendant search miss a real maintenance child (detector flakes/false-pass) or the primary test mis-parse top-level commit sids.","CI git with a different gc.auto threshold or maintenance scheduling fails to spawn maintenance-as-child in the detector run, making the red case non-deterministic."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an explicit Git-version assumption/pin to the plan and verify (e.g. a one-off Trace2 dump on the CI image) that `git maintenance run --auto` appears with a nested sid under `git commit` on the CI git before relying on the detector; alternatively gate the detector on the presence of at least one nested maintenance sid to fail closed if nesting semantics change.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.6667,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Build the new sid-ancestry helper on top of the existing `_trace_events()` iterator in `tests/_git_upkeep.py` (reuse the JSON-line parse) rather than re-implementing trace-line parsing a third time.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.7025,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["tests/_git_upkeep.py:106 `_trace_events(trace)` is a generic 'every well-formed event in a GIT_TRACE2_EVENT log' iterator","tests/unit/test_init_leaves_no_detached_upkeep.py:43-55 `_recorded_commands` re-implements the same splitlines/json.loads/JSONDecodeError loop","The novel part (sid-prefix ancestry of commit -> maintenance/gc/repack descendants) is genuinely new and NOT provided by maintenance_children(), so only the line-parsing substrate is duplicative"],"finding":"The plan's n